#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &ksnapshot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "This chapter describes the use of &ksnapshot; for capturing screen images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &ksnapshot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksnapshot; may be started by one of several ways as described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may start &ksnapshot; by selecting it from the <menuchoice> <guimenu>K-"
"Menu</guimenu><guisubmenu>Graphics</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>&ksnapshot; "
"(Screen Capture Program)</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "You may start &ksnapshot; by entering the following at the command prompt:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>%</prompt> <command>ksnapshot &amp;</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mini command line (invoked with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo>) may also be used to start &ksnapshot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once &ksnapshot; starts, you will see a window like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:148 index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksnapshot; Preview Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "Taking A Snapshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksnapshot; grabs an image of your entire desktop immediately after it is "
"started, but before it displays itself on screen. This allows you to quickly "
"create full-desktop screenshot images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The snapshot taken by &ksnapshot; is displayed in the preview window, which "
"is located in the upper left of the &ksnapshot; application window. Below is "
"an example of the preview window from &ksnapshot;. Your preview will differ "
"depending on what you have displayed on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The snapshot can be saved by clicking on the <guibutton>Save As...</"
"guibutton> button. This opens the standard &kde; save dialog, where you can "
"choose the filename, the folder location, and the format that your snapshot "
"will be saved in. If multiple snapshots are taken, the filename is "
"automatically incremented to prevent you from overwriting previous "
"snapshots. You may however edit the filename to anything you wish, including "
"the name of a previously saved snapshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To take a snapshot of a single window, select the <guilabel>Window Under "
"Cursor</guilabel> combo box entry (next to the <guilabel>Capture mode:</"
"guilabel> label), and then click on the <guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your <guilabel>Snapshot delay:</guilabel> settings you get "
"either a cross as the mouse pointer (for <guilabel>No delay</guilabel>), or "
"a standard mouse cursor which you can use to work with a program until the "
"delay is over and a snapshot is taken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <guilabel>No delay</guilabel>, the snapshot is taken immediately when "
"you click into a window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksnapshot; will display the new snapshot in the preview area, at which time "
"you can choose to save the new image (by pressing <guibutton>Save As...</"
"guibutton>) or to grab a new one, by pressing the <guibutton>New Snapshot</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To take a new snapshot of the entire desktop, select the <guilabel>Full "
"Screen</guilabel> combo box entry and then click on the <guibutton>New "
"Snapshot</guibutton> button. &ksnapshot; will now capture the entire desktop "
"if you press <guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similarly, to take a snapshot of a region, select the <guilabel>Region</"
"guilabel> combo box entry and set the <guilabel>Snapshot delay</guilabel> to "
"<guilabel>No delay</guilabel>, and then click on the <guibutton>New "
"Snapshot</guibutton> button. The mouse cursor will then change into a cross, "
"and you can then use the mouse to select the region you want to capture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To take a new snapshot of a section of a window, select the "
"<guilabel>Section of Window</guilabel> combo box entry and then click on the "
"<guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton> button. With <guilabel>No delay</"
"guilabel> you get a cross as the mouse pointer and you have to click once "
"with the &LMB; into the window. The section of the window under the mouse "
"cursor is now highlighted with a red border. Move the mouse to the wanted "
"section and click the &LMB; to capture the screenshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Snapshot Delay"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Snapshot Delay:</guilabel> box allows you to enter an "
"arbitrary time delay, in seconds, between the time that you press the "
"<guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton> button and the time that the snapshot is "
"taken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a delay time has been set, you do not have to click the mouse button to "
"capture a screenshot. This enables you to open a drop down menu, and take a "
"picture of it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exclude Window decorations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Include window decorations</guilabel> is enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you only want to capture the application itself without the surrounding "
"window decoration, disable this option and take a new snapshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Print"
msgstr "Estampar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you want to print your snapshot from the preview, just click "
"<guibutton>Print...</guibutton> and you get the standard &kde; Print dialog, "
"from where you can directly print your snapshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy to Clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you want to edit your snapshot in a graphics application without saving "
"the snapshot, just click <guibutton>Copy to Clipboard</guibutton> and insert "
"the image into a viewer or graphics application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid "Buttons"
msgstr "Botons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two further buttons located at the bottom of the &ksnapshot; "
"window. There function is described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr "Ajuda"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Gives you a menu where you can open the <guimenuitem>&ksnapshot; Handbook</"
"guimenuitem>, report a bug or get some more information <guimenuitem>About "
"&ksnapshot;</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>About &kde;</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quit"
msgstr "Quitar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quits the &ksnapshot; application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "&DCOP; Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksnapshot; can be scripted using its &DCOP; interface. This chapter "
"explains the various &DCOP; calls that you can use, and provides some "
"examples of how you can use them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As with all &DCOP; calls, you need to specify the application you want to "
"interface with, and the particular interface. With &ksnapshot; you need to "
"identify which particular application, which is <literal>ksnapshot-</"
"literal> followed by the process number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To start &ksnapshot; and obtain the right argument, use <command>dcopstart "
"ksnapshot</command>, which returns the argument (such as "
"<computeroutput>ksnapshot-20594</computeroutput>) on standard output."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can get a list of the available &DCOP; interfaces, use the right "
"arguments, as shown in this example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop `dcopstart ksnapshot` interface</"
"command><computeroutput>\n"
"QCStringList interfaces()\n"
"QCStringList functions()\n"
"QString url()\n"
"void slotGrab()\n"
"void slotPrint()\n"
"void slotSave()\n"
"bool save(QString filename)\n"
"void slotSaveAs()\n"
"void slotCopy()\n"
"void setTime(int newTime)\n"
"int timeout()\n"
"void setURL(QString newURL)\n"
"void setGrabMode(int grab)\n"
"int grabMode()\n"
"void slotMovePointer(int x,int y)\n"
"void exit()\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the examples following, the process is always <computeroutput>ksnapshot-"
"23151</computeroutput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "&DCOP; Access to Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each of the settings that you can control with the &GUI;, you can both "
"obtain the current status of that setting, and modify the setting, using "
"&DCOP;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can obtain the current capture mode using <literal>grabMode</literal>, "
"as shown below: <screen width=\"60\">\n"
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface grabMode</"
"command>\n"
"</screen> This will return <computeroutput>0</computeroutput> for full-"
"screen capture, <computeroutput>1</computeroutput> for window capture, and "
"<computeroutput>2</computeroutput> for region capture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set the capture mode using <literal>setGrabMode</literal>, which "
"requires an argument to identify the mode required (as for "
"<literal>grabMode</literal>). So you can set window capture mode "
"(<command>1</command>), using:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface setGrabMode 1</"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can obtain the current timeout setting (the <guilabel>Snapshot delay:</"
"guilabel> &GUI; item) using <literal>timeout</literal>, as shown below: "
"<screen width=\"60\">\n"
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface timeout</"
"command>\n"
"</screen> This will return the timeout setting in seconds, or zero if there "
"is no delay (capture on click)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set the timeout using <literal>setTime</literal>, which requires an "
"argument to identify the timeout duration. So you can set a delay of 4 "
"seconds using:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface setTime 4</"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can obtain the path that the snapshot will be saved to using "
"<literal>url</literal>, as shown below: <screen width=\"60\">\n"
"<prompt>$</prompt><command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface url</command>\n"
"</screen> This will return the filename, as a &URL; (eg as "
"<computeroutput>file:///home/bradh/test2.png</computeroutput>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set the path using <literal>setURL</literal>, which requires a "
"string argument to identify the new path. So you can set the path to "
"<literal>file:///home/bradh/snapshot.jpg</literal> using:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface setURL file:///"
"home/bradh/snapshot.jpg</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Taking Screenshots with &DCOP;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The key to taking screenshots with &DCOP; is use of <literal>slotGrab</"
"literal>, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface slotGrab</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will take a snapshot using the current snapshot mode and timeout "
"settings (as described above). If you want to save the snapshot image, there "
"are a number of calls you can use. If you just want to save the image to the "
"current path (as returned by <literal>url</literal> or changed by "
"<literal>setURL</literal>), you can use <literal>slotSave</literal>, as "
"shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface slotSave</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want the user to be able to specify a filename (and path), you can "
"use <literal>slotSaveAs</literal>, which will bring up a standard &kde; file "
"save dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to save the image to a different name (or path) without changing "
"the path with <literal>setURL</literal>, you can use <literal>save</"
"literal>, providing the &URL; to save to as an argument. So if you want to "
"save the snapshot to <filename>file:///tmp/tempshot.png</filename>, you can "
"do the following: <screen width=\"60\">\n"
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface save file:///tmp/"
"tempshot.png</command>\n"
"</screen> Note that this will return true if the snapshot was successfully "
"saved, and false otherwise. Also, you should be aware that if the file "
"already exists, the user will get a standard &kde; dialog that requires the "
"user to decide whether to overwrite or not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to saving the snapshot, you can also copy it to the clipboard, "
"using <literal>slotCopy</literal>, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface slotCopy</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you need to select a window that may not be under the mouse cursor, you "
"can use <literal>slotMovePointer</literal>, passing the x position (in "
"screen pixels) and the y position (also in screen pixels) as arguments. So "
"to move the mouse to the top left hand corner of the screen (0,0), you can "
"do the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface slotMoveMouse 0 "
"0</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Printing Screenshots with &DCOP;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can print the current screenshot (which may or may not have been saved) "
"using <literal>printSlot</literal>, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface slotPrint</"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that this will bring up the normal &kde; print dialog, which may "
"require user interaction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "&DCOP; Application control"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can cause &ksnapshot; to exit by using <literal>exit</literal>, as shown "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>$</prompt> <command>dcop ksnapshot-23151 interface exit</command>"
msgstr ""

